{"id": "q0016", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "aggressive", "tier": "aggressive", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 1527128380, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "c1188d4ab398808355719c420f025bd920b27aba798f5596eb328457a751cc63", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.5533501505851746, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 5, "query": "Michael is traveling on the interstate at an average speed of 50km/hr (taking into account all the necessary stops for gas, relaxation, etc.). If he goes on like this for 3 days, and the distance between Alaska and Texas is 6000 km, what percentage of this distance has he covered?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0016.wav", "input_sha256": "3c89607bb8d14da214dce2b99310b8126be8a36531e871d7245bb59d00420028", "input_samples": 355400, "input_s": 22.212, "n_real_chunks": 23, "score": 0.202, "act": 0.999, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "So if he's traveling at an average speed of 50 kilometers per hour for three days, that' s going to be 3 days times 2 4 hours a day, which is 7 2 hours. And then 7 2 hours multiplied by his speed of 5 0 kilometers per hour gives us 36 00 kilometers covered over those three days. The total distance between Alaska and Texas is 6 000 kilometers. So the percentage covered would be 3 6 00 divided by 6 0 00, which equals 0. 6 or 6 0%. So Michael has covered 60% of the distance between Al aska and Texas after three days of travel.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 22, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 42, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/