{"id": "q0034", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "aggressive", "tier": "aggressive", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2268996242, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "c1188d4ab398808355719c420f025bd920b27aba798f5596eb328457a751cc63", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.5533501505851746, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 5, "query": "Tim spends 6 hours each day at work answering phones.  It takes him 15 minutes to deal with a call.  How many calls does he deal with during his 5 day work week?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0034.wav", "input_sha256": "ca0b6ab3c8d0bc3737db3b0c3d3d55b3ad1a98d465f06219203fb63ddb861a21", "input_samples": 220200, "input_s": 13.762, "n_real_chunks": 14, "score": 0.1107, "act": 0.998, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "So he's working six hours a day, that's 3 60 minutes. And it takes him 15 minutes per call. So 3 6 0 divided by 15 is 2 4 calls a day. So in five days, that' s 24 times 5, which is 1 2 0 calls.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 13, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 20, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0034_aggressive_local.wav", "sha256": "a91185f28e36494784adf8fa0e92e5b21f15c2a73d7da87698b21e6b4500e9b1", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 19.56}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.045, 1.082, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.045, 2.083, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.046, 3.084, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.046, 4.086, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 5.0, 5.047, 5.086, 1, 0, 0], [5, 1, 6.0, 6.046, 6.086, 1, 0, 0], [6, 1, 7.0, 7.047, 7.086, 1, 0, 0], [7, 1, 8.0, 8.047, 8.087, 1, 0, 0], [8,