{"id": "q0049", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "aggressive", "tier": "aggressive", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3067005160, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "c1188d4ab398808355719c420f025bd920b27aba798f5596eb328457a751cc63", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.5533501505851746, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 5, "query": "A tower is made out of 4 blue blocks, twice as many yellow blocks, and an unknown number of red blocks. If there are 32 blocks in the tower in total, how many red blocks are there?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0049.wav", "input_sha256": "745b9d04723439e3c954057629fc4bd25d16c5666e3a5a25682ab0b36d38a651", "input_samples": 240000, "input_s": 15.0, "n_real_chunks": 15, "score": 0.0594, "act": 0.9977, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "There are four blue blocks. T wice as many yellow block s means there are eight yellow blocks. So far, that's 12 blocks accounted for. The tower has 32 blocks in total. So the number of red blocks is thirty-two minus twelve, which equal s twenty. There are twenty red blocks.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 15, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 19, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0049_aggressive_local.wav", "sha256": "aae772622be5b4f81b4d416187a967618c8d2da7b5ced49ddf68230427b0448c", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 19.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.045, 1.083, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.047, 2.085, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.047, 3.085, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.046, 4.086, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 5.0, 5.046, 5.086, 1, 0, 0], [5, 1, 6.0,