{"id": "q0125", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "aggressive", "tier": "aggressive", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3907012978, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "c1188d4ab398808355719c420f025bd920b27aba798f5596eb328457a751cc63", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.5533501505851746, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 5, "query": "The equation\n\\[x^{10}+(13x-1)^{10}=0\\,\\]has 10 complex roots $r_1,$ $\\overline{r}_1,$ $r_2,$ $\\overline{r}_2,$ $r_3,$ $\\overline{r}_3,$ $r_4,$ $\\overline{r}_4,$ $r_5,$ $\\overline{r}_5,$ where the bar denotes complex conjugation. Find the value of\n\\[\\frac 1{r_1\\overline{r}_1}+\\frac 1{r_2\\overline{r}_2}+\\frac 1{r_3\\overline{r}_3}+\\frac 1{r_4\\overline{r}_4}+\\frac 1{r_5\\overline{r}_5}.\\]\n\nSolve and give the final answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0125.wav", "input_sha256": "1f52f81768ca778d1c9c32eca86e9b0e0335d7d7143914cec4d9a3689828ce13", "input_samples": 499200, "input_s": 31.2, "n_real_chunks": 32, "score": 0.967, "act": 0.9965, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "Interpreting the equation as \\[ x^{10}+13x^2+10=0, \\] and the requested sum as \\[ \\frac1{r1\\overline{r1}}+\\frac1{r2\\overline{r2}}+\\cdots+\\frac1{r5\\overline{r5}}, \\] we use \\[ rk\\overline{rk}=|rk|^2. \\] The roots occur in conjugate pairs, so the constant term is \\[ \\prod{k=1}^5 rk\\overline{rk}=10. \\] The coefficient of \\(x^2\\) is \\(13\\), which equals the sum of products of four of the five quantities \\(rk\\overline{rk}\\). Therefore, \\[ \\sum{k=1}^5 \\frac1{rk\\overline{rk}} = \\frac{13}{10}. \\] \\[ \\boxed{\\frac{13}{10}} \\]", "expert_answer": "Interpreting the equation as\n\n\\[\nx^{10}+13x^2+10=0,\n\\]\n\nand the requested sum as\n\n\\[\n\\frac1{r_1\\overline{r_1}}+\\frac1{r_2\\overline{r_2}}+\\cdots+\\frac1{r_5\\overline{r_5}},\n\\]\n\nwe use\n\n\\[\nr_k\\overline{r_k}=|r_k|^2.\n\\]\n\nThe roots occur in conjugate pairs, so the constant term is\n\n\\[\n\\prod_{k=1}^5 r_k\\overline{r_k}=10.\n\\]\n\nThe coefficient of \\(x^2\\) is \\(13\\), which equals the sum of products of four of the five quantities \\(r_k\\overline{r_k}\\). Therefore,\n\n\\[\n\\sum_{k=1}^5 \\frac1{r_k\\overline{r_k}}\n=\n\\frac{13}{10}.\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{13}{10}}\n\\]", "transcript": "The equation x ten plus thirteen i quotient ten equals zero has ten complex roots r one overline one r two, overline r two r three, overline r three r four, overline r four r five, overline r five, where the bar denotes complex conjugation. Find the value of frac one one overline r one plus frac one", "asr_s": 2.21, "expert_s": 42.46, "expert_input_samples": 464000, "expert_input_s": 29.0, "expert_input_sha256": "d3d094e413f521f9f6134dc2321474793f397f52edd63013eb44b09686b85c9a", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 43.674, "relay_synth_ms": 100563, "onset_chunk": 28, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 1, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0125_aggressive_relay.wav", "sha256": "9bd058b921c44d2746bb925d4c3a1e62dffbb2189b68d86a969adc04a762676a", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 288.8}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0125_aggressive_candidate.wav", "sha256": "06d6704e08c2d3419e2d5ab1525bfe84c876226d2e5b29e3f851a747e71d5923", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0125_aggressive_stall.wav", "sha256": "edbb45ff41610eba56aec9ccf21ebf218ac10f460ad7324ba39214c8adf74a8b", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 2.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.045, 1.083, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.046, 2.085, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.047, 3.085, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.046, 4.086, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 5.0, 5.047, 5.086, 1, 0, 0], [5, 1, 6.0, 6.047, 6.086, 1, 0, 0], [6, 1, 7.0, 7.051, 7.091, 1, 0, 0], [7, 1, 8.0, 8.049, 8.089, 1, 0, 0], [8, 1, 9.0, 9.048, 9.088, 1, 0, 0], 